# Why These Labs Were Selected

The purpose of this section is not to reproduce the entire Pre Security curriculum.

Instead, these labs were selected because together they demonstrate a progression from:

```text
Computer Fundamentals
        ↓
Operating Systems
        ↓
Command Line
        ↓
Software & Programming
        ↓
Networking / Web
        ↓
Security Concepts
        ↓
Offensive Security
        ↓
Defensive Security
```

This provides a representative snapshot of the practical foundation developed before moving into more specialised cybersecurity training.

---

# Evidence

Each lab will include supporting screenshots where appropriate.

Evidence is intended to demonstrate genuine interaction with the practical environment without publishing:

* Flags
* Passwords
* Tokens
* Private information
* Sensitive target information
* Complete room solutions

The objective is to demonstrate **practical capability and understanding**, not reproduce the training material.

---

# What This Foundation Enables

The Pre Security work provides the technical foundation for my next stage of development.

Current progression:

```text
Pre Security
     ↓
SEC0 ✅
     ↓
NCFE Level 3 Cyber Security Practices
     +
CompTIA Security+ Study
     +
TryHackMe Security 101
     ↓
Penetration Testing
     ↓
Advanced Offensive Security
     ↓
Red Team
```

Defensive knowledge will continue to be developed alongside offensive security because understanding how systems are protected, monitored and attacked provides a more rounded security perspective.

---

# Next Stage

**TryHackMe Security 101 — In Progress**

The focus now moves from general technical foundations towards more dedicated cybersecurity knowledge and practical security skills.

Future lab documentation will prioritise environments involving:

* Linux
* Windows
* Virtual machines
* Networking
* Web applications
* Enumeration
* Vulnerability assessment
* Security tools
* Exploitation
* Privilege escalation

The emphasis will increasingly shift from **understanding systems** to **testing their security**.
